      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Alembic Mental Model and Setup",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Alembic Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Alembic== = migration tool for SQLAlchemy",
                "Chain of revision scripts, linear or branched",
                "Each has `revision` and `down_revision` IDs",
                "`alembic_version` table holds the one applied ==head== ID"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "a1b2",
                    "sub": "down_revision None",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "c3d4",
                    "sub": "down_revision a1b2",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "e5f6",
                    "sub": "head, stored in DB",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Setup",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "alembic init alembic",
                "alembic init -t async alembic"
              ],
              "note": "second form = async template"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Creates `alembic.ini`, `env.py`, `script.py.mako`, `versions/`",
                "Set `sqlalchemy.url` in the ini, or override in env.py",
                "`config.set_main_option(\"sqlalchemy.url\", settings.db_url)`",
                "{red:Never} commit real credentials in `alembic.ini`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Alembic vs create_all()",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "create_all()",
                "Alembic"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Existing tables",
                  "skipped",
                  "altered"
                ],
                [
                  "Column changes",
                  "never",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "Version tracking",
                  "none",
                  "`alembic_version`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Not a migration tool",
              "text": "`create_all()` only creates ==missing tables==. It never alters or tracks versions."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not create_all()?** It never alters tables or tracks versions",
                "**Where is DB state?** `alembic_version`, holding the head ID",
                "**Safe URL?** Override in env.py from app settings"
              ],
              "style": "star",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
