    {
      "title": "Autogenerate Workflow and Its Limits",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Autogenerate Workflow and Its Limits",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Generate a Draft",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "alembic revision --autogenerate -m \"add user email\""
              ],
              "note": "diffs target_metadata against the DB, writes a script to versions/"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Output is a ==draft==, not a guarantee",
                "**Read and edit** the script before `alembic upgrade`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Detects vs Misses",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Detects",
                "Misses"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Added or removed tables and columns",
                  "Table or column {red:renames}"
                ],
                [
                  "Nullable changes",
                  "Most `server_default` changes"
                ],
                [
                  "Indexes and unique constraints",
                  "CHECK constraints on some backends"
                ],
                [
                  "Foreign keys",
                  "Enum value changes"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Fix by Hand",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Data migrations and backfills are ==never generated==",
                "Use `op.execute()` or `bulk_insert`",
                "Rename with `op.alter_column(..., new_column_name=...)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Add nullable",
                    "sub": "add_column",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backfill",
                    "sub": "op.execute",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Set NOT NULL",
                    "sub": "alter_column",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "op.alter_column(\"users\", \"mail\", new_column_name=\"email\")",
                "op.add_column(\"users\", sa.Column(\"plan\", sa.String(), nullable=True))",
                "op.execute(\"UPDATE users SET plan = 'free'\")",
                "op.alter_column(\"users\", \"plan\", nullable=False)"
              ],
              "note": "rename keeps data; NOT NULL in three steps"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Renames",
              "text": "Autogenerate sees a rename as ==drop plus add==, so the column's data is **lost**. Edit the script."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Upgrade, Downgrade and Naming",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Upgrade, Downgrade and Naming",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Moving the Version",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`alembic upgrade head`",
                  "Applies ==all pending== revisions"
                ],
                [
                  "`alembic upgrade +1`",
                  "Applies **one** revision"
                ],
                [
                  "`alembic upgrade <rev>`",
                  "Targets one revision; a unique prefix works"
                ],
                [
                  "`alembic downgrade -1`",
                  "Reverts **one** step"
                ],
                [
                  "`alembic downgrade base`",
                  "Reverts ==everything=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rollbacks need a working ==downgrade()== in every revision"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Inspect State",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Shows or does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`alembic current`",
                  "Revision the DB is at"
                ],
                [
                  "`alembic history --verbose`",
                  "Full revision chain"
                ],
                [
                  "`alembic heads`",
                  "Latest revision(s) in the scripts"
                ],
                [
                  "`alembic stamp head`",
                  "Marks DB up to date, ==runs nothing=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Naming and Branches",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dated `file_template` gives ==sortable== filenames",
                "Write `-m` messages in the **imperative**: `add user email`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "ini",
              "lines": [
                "file_template = %%(year)d_%%(month).2d_%%(day).2d_%%(rev)s_%%(slug)s"
              ],
              "note": "in alembic.ini"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Multiple heads}: two branches each added a revision",
                "Fix: `alembic merge heads -m \"merge\"`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never edit applied revisions",
              "text": "Add a **new** revision instead; applied ones are history."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Async Engines and Deploying Migrations",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Async Engines and Deploying Migrations",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Async env.py",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Alembic is ==synchronous==; async drivers (`asyncpg`, `aiosqlite`) need a bridge",
                "Build `async_engine_from_config`, then `connection.run_sync(do_run_migrations)`",
                "Start from the template: `alembic init -t async alembic`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from alembic import context",
                "",
                "def do_run_migrations(connection):",
                "    context.configure(connection=connection, target_metadata=target_metadata)",
                "    with context.begin_transaction():",
                "        context.run_migrations()"
              ],
              "note": "sync part, runs inside run_sync"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import asyncio",
                "from sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import async_engine_from_config",
                "async def run_async_migrations():",
                "    engine = async_engine_from_config(config.get_section(config.config_ini_section), prefix=\"sqlalchemy.\")",
                "    async with engine.connect() as connection:",
                "        await connection.run_sync(do_run_migrations)",
                "asyncio.run(run_async_migrations())"
              ],
              "note": "async part, entry point of online mode"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Deploying Safely",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Release step",
                    "sub": "alembic upgrade head",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Run once",
                    "sub": "init job",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Start new app",
                    "sub": "all replicas",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Expand then contract",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Expand",
                    "note": "add column",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Deploy code",
                    "note": "old + new work",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Contract",
                    "note": "drop later",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Deploy rules",
              "items": [
                "Never run `upgrade head` in every replica's startup",
                "Concurrent runs race on `alembic_version`",
                "Back up before destructive changes"
              ],
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rollout overlap",
              "text": "Old and new code run ==together== during a rollout, so every migration must work for **both**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
